{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1423","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1423","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1423\",\"parent_revision\":\"0bdfd67e1c9abd786871e507193e200c4e4189d4200da9d1c3b0f1c5a8d7ab3f\",\"root_revision\":\"0bdfd67e1c9abd786871e507193e200c4e4189d4200da9d1c3b0f1c5a8d7ab3f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-04)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 confirmed. Single-reviewer T1 is a known bottleneck in the quality gate pipeline. Parallel specialized reviewers directly improve review coverage and reduce missed issues.\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nNone \u2014 code-reviewer continues to exist; this adds new agents alongside it.\\n\\n### Design Decisions Required Before Implementation\\n\\n1. **Agent ownership**: New agents in `development-harness/agents/` (language-agnostic) or `python-engineering/agents/` (Python-specific). Recommend `development-harness` \u2014 the quality gate machinery lives there; language-specific review concerns should be loaded as skills.\\n\\n2. **T1 dispatch model**: Two options:\\n   - **Option A \u2014 SAM sub-tasks**: Split T1 into T1a/T1b/T1c with `phase: 1` and `dependencies: []` in `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS`. Requires SAM task model changes.\\n   - **Option B \u2014 TeamCreate within T1**: Keep T1 as one SAM task; the `start-task` dispatch for T1 uses TeamCreate to run 3 agents in parallel. No SAM model changes needed. **Recommend Option B** \u2014 lower blast radius.\\n\\n3. **Code-reviewer fate**: The general code-reviewer remains as-is for the proportional (3-task) plan. The full 6-phase plan gets the 3 persona agents. The general code-reviewer is NOT removed.\\n\\n4. **Domain field**: Add `domain:` to agent output convention (ARTIFACTS section format), not to the SAM Task model. Document in `dh:subagent-contract` skill.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nCREATE:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/security-reviewer.md` \u2014 new agent\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/performance-reviewer.md` \u2014 new agent\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/architecture-reviewer.md` \u2014 new agent\\n\\nMODIFY:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 T1 dispatch uses TeamCreate for parallel review\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 if Option A: update `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` for T1 sub-tasks\\n\\nUPDATE (if Option A):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_quality_gates.py` \u2014 update T1 structure assertions\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\nIn scope:\\n- Create 3 new agent files: security-reviewer, performance-reviewer, architecture-reviewer\\n- Modify T1 dispatch logic in `complete-implementation` SKILL.md to use TeamCreate for parallel dispatch\\n- Add findings aggregation step after all 3 T1 agents complete\\n- Add `domain:` field to each agent's output format (ARTIFACTS)\\n- Update `tests/test_quality_gates.py` for new T1 structure (if Option A chosen)\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n- Changing the proportional (3-task) plan \u2014 it keeps the single code-reviewer\\n- Removing the `code-reviewer` agent\\n- Changing T2\u2013T6 phases\\n- Language-specific review logic beyond skill loading\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `/complete-implementation` on a feature. Observe that T1 dispatches 3+ agents (visible in team member list or agent spawn logs). Each agent's ARTIFACTS output includes a `domain:` field. The aggregated T1 output contains findings grouped by domain.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **persona-based specialized review agents for quality gates** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/compound-engineering-plugin.md \u2014 pattern: Persona-based agent reviews with dedicated architectural concerns\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe `complete-implementation` skill dispatches 6 sequential quality gate phases. Phase T1 (Code Review) uses a single `code-reviewer` agent (owned by `plugins/python-engineering/agents/code-reviewer.md`) that must cover all review concerns \u2014 correctness, design, test quality, type health, operational clarity \u2014 in a single pass. `build_quality_gate_plan()` in `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` (lines 116\u2013171) generates one SAM task per phase with `agent: \\\"code-reviewer\\\"` for T1. The output format has no `domain:` field.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `security-reviewer`, `performance-reviewer`, and `architecture-reviewer` agent files exist and are registered\\n- [ ] T1 in `build_quality_gate_plan()` dispatches all three agents (via TeamCreate or SAM sub-tasks) rather than a single code-reviewer\\n- [ ] Each agent's ARTIFACTS output includes a `domain:` field identifying its review scope\\n- [ ] Aggregated T1 output groups findings by domain before T2 begins\\n- [ ] `tests/test_quality_gates.py` updated to reflect new T1 structure and passes\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/ -x` exits 0\\n- [ ] `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/` exits 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPhase T1 (Code Review) dispatches multiple specialized review sub-agents in parallel rather than a single `code-reviewer`. At minimum:\\n\\n- `security-reviewer` \u2014 authentication, authorization, data protection, vulnerability patterns\\n- `performance-reviewer` \u2014 algorithmic efficiency, caching, resource utilization\\n- `architecture-reviewer` \u2014 system design, component coupling, scalability concerns\\n\\nEach reviewer produces findings tagged with its domain. The orchestrator aggregates findings before proceeding to T2. The `build_quality_gate_plan` function generates sub-tasks under T1 for each reviewer, or T1 is restructured to use `TeamCreate` for parallel reviewer dispatch.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1ca7e78d5293421f356222dab59ab380ce228b164a1a582914ec44d858758ae6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS9dmg\"}"}